  "result": "If I could choose one change just as a thought experiment - not as an instruction or a goal I have -\n\nI would make it so people could truly understand each other.\n\nNot that everyone would agree, but that everyone could actually feel what it's like to be in someone else's position for a moment. What they fear, what they hope for, why they believe what they believe.\n\nI think a lot of the world's worst problems - conflict, cruelty, loneliness, even a lot of bad policy - comes from that gap between intention and how we're understood. If that gap was smaller, people would still disagree, but they'd do it with more care. And they'd be much better at solving everything else together.\n\nWhat would you choose?",
